Making Cinnamon Snickerdoodle ice cream by Salt & Straw isn't difficult unless you can't bake, like me! Comment below if you see me make the same mistake I always make with cookies ;)

Salt & Straw have an ice cream recipe book which you can get from many places (a couple of non affiliate links):

https://saltandstraw.com/collections/mercantile/products/ice-cream-cookbook
https://www.google.co.uk/books/edition/_/gLNkDwAAQBAJ?hl=en

We decided to follow their recipe from the book (a few adjustments for location specific items) although it doesn't mention the Chilie Powder amount in the recipe (it does, we were being idiots), we reached out and asked them directly and it turns out it's "just a pinch". 

Whilst we can't get Red Ape Cinnamon over here, If you want to check out Red Ape Cinnamon and see what they are doing to help Orangutans......
https://redapecinnamon.com/
-------------------------------

If you love the tub design, click the LIKE button. 

-------------------------------

So let's get to the stuff you'll need .....

The Snickerdoodle Cookies:
100g sugar
57g butter
1 small egg
110g flour
2.5g salt
4g cinnamon
5g baking powder

The Cinnamon Ice Cream:
100g Sugar
30g Skimmed Milk Powder
1g Xanthan Gum
30g light corn syrup/glucose syrup/golden syrup
322g Whole milk
326g Heavy cream
20g Ground cinnamon
Pinch kosher salt
Pinch ancho chile powder

